WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.580
Sometimes, the sheer amount of quality TV
out there means that even the best shows aren't

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.170
safe from the chopping block — take NBC's
"Manifest," for example.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:12.840
The supernatural drama tells the story of
the people aboard Montego Air Flight 828,

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.419
which somehow lands five and a half years
in the future.

00:00:15.419 --> 00:00:20.390
The show's intriguing concept and exciting
plot have made it a fan favorite and, as a

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.740
result, "Manifest" has been a reliable workhorse
and one of the network's most popular shows

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:24.949
of its kind.

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:29.519
Unfortunately, the world of small-screen entertainment
is a volatile place, and even these considerable

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:32.250
accolades weren't enough to keep "Manifest"
afloat.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.760
Recent news indicates that NBC has opted against
greenlighting "Manifest" Season 4, and as

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.060
such, the show is pretty much history.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:45.350
"No, no, no…"

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:49.070
This means there's a very real chance that
fans will never find out exactly what happened

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:52.620
to the people aboard the fateful flight — which
is all the more frustrating when you consider

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.870
that the ending of Season 3 added a seemingly
never-ending line of cliffhangers to the already

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.590
impressive mountain of mysteries.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:02.440
Despite this, the show's fate appears to have
been sealed, so for now, there's only one

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.700
real mystery that needs to be solved: Why
on Earth was "Manifest" canceled in the first

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:07.700
place?

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.700
"It makes no sense."

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.289
Now, if you think that the cancellation news
came as a bit of a surprise to fans, "Manifest"

00:01:13.289 --> 00:01:15.649
creator Jeff Rake certainly agrees.

00:01:15.649 --> 00:01:17.490
After the hammer dropped, he tweeted...

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:21.499
"My dear Manifesters, I'm devastated by NBC's
decision to cancel us.

00:01:21.499 --> 00:01:24.829
That we've been shut down in the middle is
a gut punch to say the least.

00:01:24.829 --> 00:01:25.979
Hoping to find a new home.

00:01:25.979 --> 00:01:28.729
You the fans deserve an ending to your story.

00:01:28.729 --> 00:01:31.530
Thanks for the love shown to me, cast, and
crew."

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:35.490
He also included the hashtag "savemanifest,"
which might very well see a fair amount of

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.650
use in the future.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.780
The news of the show's grim fate arrived on
June 14, and as Deadline reported, the die

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:43.520
was cast shortly before the actors' options
expired.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.499
This, of course, means that "Manifest" only
got halfway through its planned six-season

00:01:47.499 --> 00:01:48.499
arc.

00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:49.520
"But why?"

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.930
As for why anyone could even consider canceling
a seemingly successful show like "Manifest"

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:56.430
in the first place, the answer is still up
in the air.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:00.789
However, TV Series Finale has noted that the
show's third season didn't manage to attract

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:05.290
quite as many viewers as the previous two,
to the point that its ratings dropped 31 percent

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.740
in the 18 to 49 demographic.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.110
Still, considering that "Manifest" was nevertheless
quite popular, the decision not to renew it

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.940
couldn't have been an easy one — which could
explain why the network waited until the last

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.850
moments to pull the plug.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.150
Though "Manifest" is down for now, there's
a decent chance that it's not out.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:25.430
Obviously, the show has no shortage of plot
left — and, as Deadline notes, creator Jeff

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:29.250
Rake has made it clear that he'd still like
to wrap up the remaining three seasons.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:34.440
Likewise, Warner Bros. TV is reportedly putting
out feelers to see if the show can be rescued.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.580
Even if the series ends up finding a new home,
there may still be some wrinkles in the plan,

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:42.040
since it appears that the options of the cast
of "Manifest" have expired.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:46.040
So, regardless of what happens, a potential
return would likely have plenty of hurdles

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.920
to clear, and even a best-case scenario might
mean that fans will have to wait for quite

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.010
some time before new episodes arrive.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:56.320
Then again, fan-favorite shows of a sufficiently
high profile have been rescued from the scrap

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.530
heap before.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:01.950
The beloved sci-fi show "The Expanse" is heading
toward Season 6, because Amazon Prime picked

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.090
it up after Syfy dropped it before its fourth
season.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:09.840
NBC itself rescued the popular police sitcom
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine" in the wake of Fox cancelling

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:10.840
it.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:14.450
Hopefully, some platform or network will extend
the same courtesy to "Manifest" and all of

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.930
its unsolved mysteries.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:20.230
Luckily for fans, "Manifest" is no lemon,
and might hold plenty of allure for the right

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.230
buyer.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:24.570
In fact, before the show got the ax, it was
trending on Netflix.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.960
Time will tell if this means that the streaming
platform is interested in further seasons

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:31.180
of the show, but it may not be outside the
realm of possibility.

